WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:01.480 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  Overland is your typical family road  trip if that road trip included tons of  monsters and some highway robbery  the premise is rather simple you begin  your journey on the East Coast and you  need to get to the west coast  unfortunately civilization is in  shambles and fungal looking creatures  have sprung up from the ground and of  course the poor souls who've managed to  survive aren't the most trustworthy of  folk part Fire Emblem and part Oregon  Trail Overland is a randomly generated  tactical adventure game that has you  traveling from area to area scrounging  for gas supplies weapons and meeting  fellow survivors  once you've looted an area you can drive  on out and continue your journey across  the United States but that sounds easier  than it is if you run out of gas you'll  end up stranded on the side of the road  surrounded by monsters if you leave your  car unattended another survivor could  steal it and you'll be forced to  continue on foot  if you get surrounded in your car you'll  be forced to fight your way out and if  everyone in your party dies then it's  game over combat against both humans and  monsters resembles a simplified tactical  adventure game each character can travel  a certain amount of tiles per turn to  gather supplies or attack enemies  unlike XCOM or fire emblem though these  interactions are rather simple survivors  all have the same based attack and  there's not a leveling system most  enemies only take a few hits to kill but  so do your survivors this makes  positioning key as you scour the area  for supplies in most cases though it's  best to avoid combat altogether supplies  are limited in fragile bottles for  example can be used as weapons but will  break after one attack and since the  bigger enemies take more than one hit to  kill your best bet is to stay out of  their way and make for a quick exit  there's also an element of stealth to  encounters if you leave the car running  the monsters will hear you if you move  to breathe the monsters will hear you  and of course if you fight a monster or  break a bottle the monsters will hear  you because only dogs can fight back  empty-handed you need to be quiet and  plan your approach defensively if you do  manage to clear a path to the exit you  can hop in your car and escape as long  as you have enough gas from here you are  taken to a world map where you can pick  your next destination most of the time  you are given two options some of these  places are high-risk and offer better  rewards while others are safe but have  fewer resources while others may have  survivors which can either be a deadly  encounter or a safe haven managing  resources in planning your moves becomes  crucial should I send Steven out to  fetch more gas while Andrew leaves the  car running or should they go together  will Hillary have enough time to grab  that med kit before the monster catches  her my car only fits three and I have  four survivors  who do I leave behind  these are the kind of questions you'll  be asking yourself every step of the way  you'll be constantly weighing the risks  against the rewards and if you misjudge  a situation that could be the end of  your run if you make a wrong turn and  your team gets killed off you're forced  to start from the beginning but the game  truly shines the further along you get  you get more and more desperate as the  monsters start to greatly outnumber your  team sometimes you have to leave a  survivor behind if you want the rest of  your group to survive you feel as though  you're barely scraping by and when you  do survive against all odds it's all the  more satisfying unfortunately you will  die this can be frustrating but because  characters locales and interactions are  all randomly generated every playthrough  has its own unique story and that means  there's always a good reason to keep  playing if this game sounds interesting  to you you can pick it up in first  access at Overland - game comm for $20  the full release is still aways out but  it's definitely worth keeping an eye on  and if you've tuned in every day this  week from my indie mix coverage thank  you so so much we love doing this kind  of stuff and we can't do it without you  if you enjoyed this video or maybe one  of the other indie mix videos consider  subscribing it really helps us out thank  you and until next time  [Music]

